WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.307
Standardization and correction should not be treated as the same operation.

00:00:04.307 --> 00:00:09.277
Trimming an email or changing case preserves the intended value.

00:00:09.277 --> 00:00:16.627
Mapping tech to Electronics may be appropriate if the business taxonomy explicitly defines that equivalence.

00:00:16.627 --> 00:00:22.797
Changing a negative price to a positive price makes a much stronger claim about reality.

00:00:22.797 --> 00:00:25.672
That kind of correction needs evidence.

00:00:25.672 --> 00:00:32.352
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:38.012
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.012 --> 00:00:45.917
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:51.927
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:57.600
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
